nected directed graph $G$ on $n$ vertices with minimum degree at least $n$ contains a directed Hamilton cycle.\n\n## orientation ↗ reference\n\n1026 papers tagged with this keyword\n\n2026-11-02\n\nYiming Lei, Chenxi Lv, Bing Dai\n\n# • INFO • BIB • PDF • ARXIV •\n\nk-uniform l-Eulerian hypergraphs\n\nWe consider $l$-Euler trails and $l$-Euler circuits in finite $k$-uniform directed multihypergraphs, where $k\\geq 2$ and $1\\leq l<k$. Let $D$ be such a directed multihypergraph. The notions of $l$-connectivity and $l$-balance are defined in terms of the $l$-tails and $l$-heads of its hyperarcs. It is shown that $D$ is $l$-Eulerian if and only if $D$ is $l$-connected and $l$-balanced. Moreover, $D$ is $l$-semi-Eulerian if and only if $D$ is $l$-connected and has exactly two states with unequal $l$-indegrees and $l$-outdegrees, one with $l$-outdegree one greater than its $l$-indegree and the other with $l$-indegree one greater than its $l$-outdegree. The proofs are based on an $l$-transition digraph and the classical Euler theorem for directed multigraphs. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n(PDF) \\ell$-covering $k$-hypergraphs are quasi-eulerian (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/348832298_ell-covering_k-hypergraphs_are_quasi-eulerian)\nciteturn5search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.8 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; covered by any introductory graph theory course. ... In this paper, we aim to extend Theorem 1.1 to all ℓ-covering k-hypergraphs. ... Further substituting n≥ℓ+k from (5) and isolating ℓ, we obtain ℓ≤4−k ... P s(ℓ) : “Every ℓ-covering (ℓ+s)-hypergraph with at least two edges is quasi-eulerian.”\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n(PDF) Covering hypergraphs are eulerian (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/348426691_Covering_hypergraphs_are_eulerian)\nciteturn5search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.8 years ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; C=u 0 W 0 v 0 u 1